  "title": "Erdős Problem #627",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\omega(G)$ denote the clique number of $G$ and $\\chi(G)$ the chromatic number. If $f(n)$ is the maximum value of $\\chi(G)/\\omega(G)$, as $G$ ranges over all graphs on $n$ vertices, then does $ \\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{f(n)}{n/(\\log n)^2} $ exist?",
